{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/89395-missing-deities","id":89395,"title":"Missing Deities!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-12T04:55:19-07:00","id":89395,"title":"Missing Deities!","content":"First these boards are evil as I had to write this ten times in order to post! Secondly, many deities are simply missing. Figures like Dememter, Hestia, Iris, Hecate, Sekmet, Hathor, and Oya, are simply not defined. Heck they gave us a scion without a devine parent in the recent supplement (check the Tuatha). Please list major missing deities and lets see if we can inspire another web supplement covering the missing gods!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T07:12:07-07:00","id":89455,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm guessing that this is about existing books and supplements.<br /> <br /> <i>The principal gods of Greek mythology</i><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"http://www.pantheon.org/areas/genealogy/principal_greek.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://www.pantheon.org/areas/genealogy/principal_greek.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> *<span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Hephaestus is often said to be only Hera's son, and Aphrodite is usually said to be born of sea foam. </i></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> Then there's Zeus' children:<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://www.pantheon.org/areas/genealogy/zeus.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> hmm...Prometheus gets into the horny act as well;<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://www.pantheon.org/areas/genealogy/prometheus.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think the Greek Gods were too badly under-represented from the principals alone. I do think it was a bad generalization to label all Titans as evil. Prometheus was a better friend to mankind than Zeus, and I believe that Hecate has always been worshipped as a great deity in her own right before she became a tripartite goddess figure. And everyone worshipped Hestia, the embodiment of Home and Hearth whether they knew it or not.<br /> A rather curiously dry but interesting <a href=\"http://www.gutenberg.org/files/39250/39250-h/images/tree.png\" target=\"_blank\">genealogy table including the titans</a> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T07:24:50-07:00","id":89460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/89395-missing-deities#post89395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First these boards are evil as I had to write this ten times in order to post! Secondly, many deities are simply missing. Figures like Dememter, Hestia, Iris, Hecate, Sekmet, Hathor, and Oya, are simply not defined. Heck they gave us a scion without a devine parent in the recent supplement (check the Tuatha). Please list major missing deities and lets see if we can inspire another web supplement covering the missing gods!</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.gothambynight.com/scion/hestia.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Hestia!</a> <a href=\"http://www.gothambynight.com/scion/hecate.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Hecate!</a> <a href=\"http://www.gothambynight.com/scion/sekhmet.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Sekhmet!</a> <a href=\"http://www.gothambynight.com/scion/hathor.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Hathor!</a> <a href=\"http://www.gothambynight.com/scion/oya.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Oya!</a><br /> <br /> Demeter is a bit of a sore spot, since she occupies the exact same design space as Persephone and in some variations of the myth actually is Persephone. By generation she would be a Titan.<br /> <br /> Iris is probably Legend 9, which means she would only have Dexterity associated by RAW, or Psychopomp associated by GBN.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T07:55:10-07:00","id":89480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/89395-missing-deities?p=89460#post89460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.gothambynight.com/scion/hestia.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Hestia!</a> <a href=\"http://www.gothambynight.com/scion/hecate.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Hecate!</a> <a href=\"http://www.gothambynight.com/scion/sekhmet.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Sekhmet!</a> <a href=\"http://www.gothambynight.com/scion/hathor.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Hathor!</a> <a href=\"http://www.gothambynight.com/scion/oya.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Oya!</a><br /> <br /> Demeter is a bit of a sore spot, since she occupies the exact same design space as Persephone and in some variations of the myth actually is Persephone. By generation she would be a Titan.<br /> <br /> Iris is probably Legend 9, which means she would only have Dexterity associated by RAW, or Psychopomp associated by GBN.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Rainbow powers might be coming in with the Sky-Thunder split. So that might be a consideration for her as well.<br /> <br /> Hmm...I believe these three would be good additions to the Deva. The first two are widely worshipped deities with tonnes of myths and are worthy of Legend 12, while the third is a bit more hit and miss. I think she has enough to be Legend 12, but I will happily admit that YMMV in her case.<br /> <br /> 1. Durga: Goddess of war and supreme protector, whose name means 'The Invincible One', who should have Charisma, Appearance, Strength, War and Guardian. An argument could be made for Stamina, but is not essential.<br /> <br /> 2. Hanuman: Monkey God and former Scion of Vayu turned deity due to his many, many exploits in the Ramayana, he should have Strength, Dexterity, Guardian and Animal (Monkey).<br /> <br /> 3. Ganga, Goddess of the Ganges river, the most sacred of waterways to the Hindu populace. Should have Appearance, Strength and Water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T07:57:23-07:00","id":89482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/89395-missing-deities#post89395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First these boards are evil as I had to write this ten times in order to post! Secondly, many deities are simply missing. Figures like Dememter, Hestia, Iris, Hecate, Sekmet, Hathor, and Oya, are simply not defined. Heck they gave us a scion without a devine parent in the recent supplement (check the Tuatha). Please list major missing deities and lets see if we can inspire another web supplement covering the missing gods!</div> </div> </div> </div>Irusan - the missing god in question - got an <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/since-you-can-get-this-in-print-now-something-extra-for-scion-extras/\" target=\"_blank\">official web writeup</a> by Extras' author.<br /> <br /> <br /> On a sidenote about the categorisation of certain divine figures, Dave Brookshaw has mentioned God-born characters having parents that 1e would have considered Titans, like Nyx and Chronos. Which raises a lot of questions, like what they'd be considered in 2e, which side, if any, they'd be on, and whether having Titan parents will actually be a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T10:54:26-07:00","id":89574,"title":"","content":"While not a deity per say (He is listed as a god in some variations of his story) I would very much like Cerberus to at least not be listed as a goddamned Titanspawn. As a god I doubt he'd hold enough juice to be higher than a Legend 9 God since he was kinda late to the game for the variations of his story where the did make him a god. <br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind seeing Hercules actually tossed into the mix with the Dodekatheon, instead of listed as a side individual as part of a conspiracy. <br /> <br /> For the Egyptians since I can never remember how to spell their damned pantheon, wouldn't mind seeing Sekment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T11:57:57-07:00","id":89625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/89395-missing-deities?p=89574#post89574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I would very much like Cerberus to at least not be listed as a goddamned Titanspawn. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>He's listed as Titanspawn for a reason...in most depictions he <i>is</i> one, spawn of the Titans Echidna and Typhon.<br /> <br /> I really hope 2e gets rid of the assumption that all Titans and Titanspawn are inherently evil. What they are is inherently <i>alien</i>. A Water Titan literally cares more about a swimming pool than the child drowning in it. And a Titanspawn like Cerberus cares more about the rules of the dead than the needs of the living.<br /> <br /> Getting that across would also help fix situations like Danu and Geb, who by all accounts should be Titans and were only put on the God roster because they weren't evil. It will also help fix issues like the 'Where has my God gone' situation amongst the Yazata with Ahura Mazda, and complete rewriting of mythic personalities like Tethys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T12:55:35-07:00","id":89653,"title":"","content":"I can't find evidence of Cerberus being a god, either -- could someone give me a source on that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T16:54:37-07:00","id":89821,"title":"","content":"There are plenty of heroes, especially in the Greek pantheon, that could merit a book in itself. <i>&quot;Um..Hagrid? <a href=\"http://fc01.deviantart.net/fs70/i/2013/104/3/4/cerberus_by_mlappas-d4rm4h0.png\" target=\"_blank\">This is NOT Fluffy</a>!&quot;</i> I suppose if one were to revere the Guardian purview, then Cerberus, Heimdall, et al would make the grade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T17:56:30-07:00","id":89851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/89395-missing-deities?p=89653#post89653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't find evidence of Cerberus being a god, either -- could someone give me a source on that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you have my brain kicking itself. The story I read with him in it was so long ago that I don't recall the title but it was a story surrounding Kerberos (Cerberus) himself, telling of his youth and growing up. Part of the story talks about how he came to be the hound that guarded the gates of Hades, in life he befriended a small girl and they grew up together. To gain Kerberos as a guardian he sent a serpent to poison the girl while they slept. When she died Hades made a bargain with Kerberos. If he guarded the gates faithfully he would keep her in he Elysian Fields and allow her to visit him, if not she would go to Tartarus. <br /> <br /> The story later tells of how due to his faithful service as a guardian Kerberos is awarded with godhood. <br /> <br /> Now I'm really wishing that I could remember what the hell the book was called.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T20:00:45-07:00","id":89893,"title":"","content":"There were a bunch of lesser Egyptian deities listed in the Kane Chronicles trilogy, one being Bes, the dwarf god and one fugly guy. As with Percy Jackson, there were some named in the two series, both Greek and Roman. And don't forget Eris, the Greek goddess of discord and her golden apple. She would make a good counterpoint to Loki in terms of douchyness. There was also a title that I saw in a Borders long ago called, &quot;The Bull God&quot;. It's a story of how the Minotaur was once a god but was tricked into the labyrinth by the other gods for some reason or another. Might be good for an NPC lesser god. Since this game is now ongoing, if we persist, then perhaps Onyx Path will make splats detailing these deities in future sourcebooks. Plus, Pan being the form of the Devil is just Christian propaganda to convert worshipers of the Greco-Roman pantheon. Another example of confusion is when I saw an episode of No Right Answer. The topic was: &quot;Who's the Best Devil?&quot; The two contenders that they debated for in the episode was Hades in one corner and the actual Devil in the other. The concerning thing is that at the end, Hades, Greek god of the dead, was considered a better Devil, than the ACTUAL Devil himself. <br /> <br /> Sorry for rambling off topic like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T09:39:04-07:00","id":90283,"title":"","content":"I feel like a line should be drawn between works of fiction being written in modern times that are based on old myths but play with the assumptions those myths rely on and actual mythology as it stands from a scholastic/secular(?) perspective While modern works of fiction make for great inspiration for a game, the corebook doesn't seem like the place to use them, since the corebook is supposed to be more universal.<br /> <br /> The Minotaur was the product of Zeus and one of his many lovers, whom he seduced while in the form of a bull. This lady was a princess, and her father locked him (the minotaur) in the Labyrinth because it was a threat to the people / because he was ashamed of what his daughter had given birth to, depending on the tale. So while creating a bull-headed scion to run in your game would be cool, and it would be awesome if things like that were nodded to in the corebook, actually having the Minotaur as a god from which to play Scions would just be kind of odd, especially given as he only appears, really, in that one legend.<br /> <br /> On the topic of Cerberus, again, though -- since I can't find any evidence of that story <i>anywhere,</i> I'm going to go out on a limb here and presume it was pretty localized, or even fictional. I have found a series of books called &quot;the Wrath of Kerberus&quot;, but that doesn't seem to be what you're referring to be any stretch, and if I remember correctly, the way I hear it, Cerberus has been in Hades' care since he was born, being a terrible hound who's spit created wolfsbane; he was taken to the underworld where there wasn't anyone to inadvertently kill because everyone was already dead. However, again, this story could make for interesting campaign fodder -- perhaps he escapes the underworld for some reason (even well-behaved dogs get mischievous sometimes, right?), and meets a young girl who can talk to animals; meanwhile, no one's there to stop the souls of the dead from escaping. . . . and Cerberus proves himself worthy of godhood when he rounds up the dead he's let escape and brings them back to the underworld, returning to a lonely life out of duty or tragedy.<br /> <br /> However, while it would make a good story, it would not make for a very good core book.<br /> <br /> Pan and Eris, however, are both very good candidates for possible deities, though they'd be lower Legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T13:59:10-07:00","id":90413,"title":"","content":"Your correct in saying it is possible that it is a work of fiction based on the Mythology. I was younger when I read it (I think I was 15 or 16), and public libraries are sometimes sketchy as to weather a book belongs in the Mythology section or the Fiction section, and since the book dealt with Cerberus they may have put it in the Mythology section, when in fact it was a more modern interpretation that belonged in the Fiction section. But yeah even as fiction it still would be a great idea for a story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T14:09:21-07:00","id":90417,"title":"","content":"There's an entire category in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1377-fan-written-scion-material\">Fan-Written Scion Material</a> thread all about statting up extra Gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T04:41:59-07:00","id":90797,"title":"","content":"When I took a vague stab at Iris on the old White Wolf boards I pointed out that Iris had been around long enough to have been a goddess when Apollo was born. Her role in Apollo's birth is recorded in the Homeric Hynms. I suggested that Iris' Purviews were Arete (she's in that Pantheon), Epic Dex (she ran from delos to Olympus several times in one day) Sky (there are ancient liturgies were the Greeks ask Zeus and Hera to have Iris bring them rain showers and fair winds, i.e. Iris can do these things and will if Zeus and Hera ask her to) Psychopomp (because Scion: Demigod says so) and either Epic Cha or Epic App (depending on your interpretation of how she uses her charm).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 05-28-2017, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T06:51:39-07:00","id":90870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/89395-missing-deities?p=90797#post90797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I took a vague stab at Iris on the old White Wolf boards I pointed out that Iris had baan around long enough to have been a goddess when Apollo was born. Her role in Apollo's birth is recorded in the Homeric Hynms. I suggested that Iris' Purviews were Arete (she's in that Pantheon), Epic Dex (she ran for delos to Olympus several times in one day) Sky (there are ancient liturgies were the Greeks ask Zeus and Hera to have Iris bring them rain showers and fair winds, i.e. Iris can do these things and will if Zeus and Hera ask her to) Psychopomp (because Scion: Demigod says so) and either Epic Cha or Epic App (depending on your interpretation of how she uses her charm).</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW Scion handles associated powers rather poorly. You are only associated with purviews if you possess the Avatar, which is restricted to Legend 12 gods. Iris is probably not a Legend 12 goddess. Epic Attributes become associated at 8, which means she could have any number of attributes associated. But we only know she was able to run extremely fast. It is reasonable to assume she was charming or persuasive, but we have no idea how much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T08:13:58-07:00","id":90904,"title":"","content":"I don't think most people would rate Iris as a Legend 12 deity. That would affect the number of Purviews and Epics that she was able to grant to any potential offspring. Right now she's at 3 Purviews and 2 Epics. That's a lot more than several true members of the Dodekatheon (the principle 12) have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T14:36:23-07:00","id":91109,"title":"","content":"I think that is the whole crux of the whole situation in the first place, which gods to add into the book. Well for being the &quot;Core&quot; book it is unlikely that they'd add Gods that are not Legend 12 Gods, as they would severely limit what their children can learn, only to the Epic Attributes. This is of course, based on the assumption that they will keep to the formula that you must have a single boon from each level of a purview as well as the Avatar as it has been said that some mechanics will be changed. <br /> <br /> The question than really turns to &quot;Which Gods do we believe are Legend 12&quot; which can be tricky since that is something that is purely based on the opinion of the writers. After all, it'd make no sense to me to see any god who is at least as well known as Hercules is in mythology, and has been around as long as he has, as less than Legend 12 since they have both the time under their belt, as well as the popularity to support it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T05:17:59-07:00","id":91555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/89395-missing-deities?p=91109#post91109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that is the whole crux of the whole situation in the first place, which gods to add into the book. Well for being the &quot;Core&quot; book it is unlikely that they'd add Gods that are not Legend 12 Gods, as they would severely limit what their children can learn, only to the Epic Attributes. This is of course, based on the assumption that they will keep to the formula that you must have a single boon from each level of a purview as well as the Avatar as it has been said that some mechanics will be changed.<br /> <br /> The question than really turns to &quot;Which Gods do we believe are Legend 12&quot; which can be tricky since that is something that is purely based on the opinion of the writers. After all, it'd make no sense to me to see any god who is at least as well known as Hercules is in mythology, and has been around as long as he has, as less than Legend 12 since they have both the time under their belt, as well as the popularity to support it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly torn on the Associateds issue. On one hand, it is pretty bad to have to tell someone who wants to play the Scion of Iris that he gets to XP discount to Purviews. On the other hand, I love the thematic feeling that only once you achieve Avatar level of a Purview does it become a part of your ichor.<br /> <br /> Hercules/Heracles is well-known as a Hero, but he kind of drops off the map once he becomes a God. By contrast, Dionysus has adventures both pre and post-Apotheosis. So I'd wager Hercules isn't Legend 12.<br /> <br /> Of course, 'What makes a God Legend 12' is one of the great subjective debates of Scion...right up there with 'What makes something a God', so YMMV strongly on this issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T07:28:31-07:00","id":91612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/89395-missing-deities?p=91555#post91555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm honestly torn on the Associateds issue. On one hand, it is pretty bad to have to tell someone who wants to play the Scion of Iris that he gets to XP discount to Purviews. On the other hand, I love the thematic feeling that only once you achieve Avatar level of a Purview does it become a part of your ichor.<br /> <br /> Hercules/Heracles is well-known as a Hero, but he kind of drops off the map once he becomes a God. By contrast, Dionysus has adventures both pre and post-Apotheosis. So I'd wager Hercules isn't Legend 12.<br /> <br /> Of course, 'What makes a God Legend 12' is one of the great subjective debates of Scion...right up there with 'What makes something a God', so YMMV strongly on this issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>The text for <u>God</u>, and a section of <u>We are but Mere Mortals</u> described the original Titans as essentially elemental forces, and the next generation (gods) as the result of the mingling of two or more titanic elemental forces, which would make the original gods a sort of para or quasi-elemental. Then they mention that the presence of man, a being that can think and reason, created the shapes they currently wear. Given all of that, the gods were not \u201ccreated\u201d by men, but rather <b>defined</b> by men. It\u2019s after interaction with the world that the gods bother to incarnate as any one specific form, but the power has always been there nonetheless. Not that this gives us any clue as to how to compare power levels between gods who were there near the beginning (like Iris and Hecate), as opposed to those who came later (Athena or Nike).<br /> In this cosmology as described (which is a little more lovecraftian than you\u2019d expect), a scion would be nothing more than a physical incubator for a \u201clarval god\u201d. Whatever method they use to implant this seed (from rampant sex to thought materialization) results in the same kind of being, which is odd, since for some reason, a titan can\u2019t actually do the same thing the same way regardless of how obviously more powerful they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T09:40:29-07:00","id":91703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/89395-missing-deities?p=91555#post91555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm honestly torn on the Associateds issue. On one hand, it is pretty bad to have to tell someone who wants to play the Scion of Iris that he gets to XP discount to Purviews. On the other hand, I love the thematic feeling that only once you achieve Avatar level of a Purview does it become a part of your ichor.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should use a houserule that removes the XP discount from Purviews. The same is true of XP discount Knacks and Boons.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}